# Email Disposal API - Project Summary

## Overview

This project is a Docker-deployable Node.js email API with SQLite persistence. It serves random available emails from a database-backed pool and locks each returned email briefly to avoid duplicate active use.

## Stack

- Backend: Node.js, Express
- Database: SQLite via `better-sqlite3`
- Admin UI: static HTML, CSS, and vanilla JavaScript
- Deployment: Docker and Docker Compose

## Runtime

- App port: `3000` by default, configurable with `PORT`
- Data directory: `${DATA_DIR:-/app/data}`
- SQLite file: `${DATA_DIR:-/app/data}/emails.sqlite`
- Docker Compose volume: `./data:/app/data`

## Routes

- `GET /api/email`: returns and locks one available email.
- `GET /api/email.php`: compatibility alias for the old PHP path.
- `GET /admin/`: static admin panel.
- `GET /admin/quick_stats.php`: admin stats JSON.
- `POST /admin/bulk_operations.php`: import emails, clear locks, delete all emails.
- `GET /admin/export_emails.php`: text export of all emails.

## Data Policy

The app creates the SQLite schema on startup but does not auto-import `data/email.txt` or `data/emails.txt`. Use the admin import flow to load emails.

## Verification

Use:

```bash
npm test
npm run lint
docker compose build
```

Docker may be unavailable in some local WSL environments until Docker Desktop integration is enabled.
